				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fastandbulbous" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2139686); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2139686&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607158709" alt="fastandbulbous" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2139686)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/fastandbulbous" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2139686); return false;" >fastandbulbous</a></span> <span class="odate time_1602026198 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Oct 2020 23:16</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4790290">
									

<p>Hello SCPeople,</p>
<p>In this thread, everyone can chip in a few of their favorite songs that they associate with Halloween or Autumn, along with a small prompt about why they're your favorite. Then, when the big day rolls around, I'll make a playlist of everybody's songs and a document with all of your prompts. I'm not aware that something like this has been done before, and I think it can be a fun way to take a snapshot of the SCP community and its inhabitants as we are now!</p>
<p>It's very simple in concept, but of course we could make it as fancy and fun as we want!<br />
As far as what kinds of songs are allowed, there are <em>basically</em> no rules - anything from your favorite black metal dirge to a song you remember listening to on Halloween night as kid. You can even get memey with it, if you so choose! I only ask that if there are dark themes in the song, you provide appropriate Trigger Warnings. Since I'm sure some of you have a hundred spooky songs that you love (this being the SCP wiki) I'd like to keep it to a limit of 3 songs per person. After a few people have contributed, I'll give my own songs :&gt;</p>
<p>Everyone should feel free to comment on other people's choices, strike up discussions, and compliment each others taste - just keep it positive!</p>
<p>Everyone have fun, and enjoy the longer nights, the falling leaves, and the howling in the woods!</p>
<p>(<a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MarBVyZVe9s">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MarBVyZVe9s</a>)</p>

